  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: thunderbird security update",
  "description": "Multiple security vulnerabilities have been identified and addressed in Mozilla Thunderbird, including numerous use-after-free flaws, sandbox escapes, privilege escalations, information disclosures, spoofing issues, and boundary condition errors across various components such as JavaScript GC, DOM, Graphics, Audio/Video, and Networking. Additionally, a vulnerability allowing feed subscriptions to leak NTLM credentials on Windows was fixed. These issues collectively pose significant risks to the confidentiality, integrity, and security isolation of the Thunderbird application.",
